 foto con el cowboy desnudo en la ciudad de Nueva York.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Original sentence: "A shirtless child plays with an adult indoors."\nTranslation to French: "Un enfant dévêtu joue avec un adulte à l\'intérieur."\nTranslation to Spanish: "Un niño sin camisa juega con un adulto dentro de casa."\nTranslation to German: "Ein nackter Kind spielt mit einem Erwachsenen drinnen."\nTranslation to Italian: "Un bambino senza camicia gioca con un adulto dentro casa."\nTranslation to Portuguese: "Um menino sem camisa brinca com um adulto dentro de casa."\nTranslation to Chinese: "" (yī gè míng xiǎo hái bù xiǎng de chāi yù yī gè dà shǒu rén zhōng nèi).'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Original sentence:  People hang upside down as a roller coaster executes a spiral loop-the-loop.\n\nTranslation to French: Les gens sont suspendus la tête en bas alors que le manège execute un boucle spirale.\n\nTranslation to Spanish: La gente cuelga cabeza abajo mientras un carrusel ejecuta un bucle en espiral.\n\nTranslation to German: Die Leute hängen kopfüber, während ein Achterbahn ein Spirallöcher durchführt.\n\nTranslation to Italian: La gente è appesa a testa in giù mentre un treno a passo doppio esegue un loop in spirale.\n\nTranslation to Portuguese: As pessoas estão penduradas de cabeça para baixo enquanto um trem de diversão executa um loop em espiral.\n\nTranslation to Chinese (Simplified): 人们头朝下悬挂着，而旋转飞车正在执行螺旋式的环形飞行。\n\nTranslation to Japanese: 人々は頭を下に向け、ローラーコースターが螺旋状のループを回している。'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: English: "People are on a roller coaster."\nFrench: "Des personnes sont sur un manège à sensations."\nSpanish: "Las personas están en un montaña rusa."\nGerman: "Menschen sind auf einer Achterbahn."'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Countries bound together by common interests, heritage or systems.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Nations united by common goals, heritage, or traditions.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Shared interests, history, or institutions have brought nations together in unity.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Shared interests, history, and institutions have brought various nations together in a unified whole.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Different countries often share a common past.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: There are countries with common goals.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Countries are united by common bonds.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Countries share common bonds.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Converting organic and inorganic materials into absorbable substances often involves various processes, including:\n\n1. **Composting**: Breaking down organic materials (e.g., food waste, leaves) into nutrient-rich compost using heat, microorganisms, and aeration.\n2. **Digestion**: Using enzymes and microorganisms to break down complex molecules (e.g., proteins, carbohydrates, fats) into simpler compounds that can be absorbed by the body.\n3. **Incineration**: Burning materials (e.g., plastics, paper) at high temperatures to produce ash and gases, which can be filtered and converted into usable substances.\n4. **Pyrolysis**: Heating materials (e.g., biomass, plastics) in the absence of oxygen to produce a mixture of gases, liquids, and solids that can be converted into fuels, chemicals, or other products.\n5. **Chemical treatment**: Using chemical reactions (e.g., hydrolysis, oxidation) to break down or transform materials into absorbable substances.\n6. **Anaerobic digestion**: Breaking down organic materials (e.g., food waste, sewage) in the absence of oxygen to produce biogas (a mixture of methane and carbon dioxide) and a nutrient-rich sludge.\n7. **Solvent extraction**: Using solvents (e.g., water, ethanol) to extract valuable compounds from materials (e.g., plant extracts, oils).\n8. **Electrolysis**: Using an electric current to break down materials (e.g., water, salt) into their constituent elements or compounds.\n9. **Microbial fermentation**: Using microorganisms (e.g., bacteria, yeast) to break down complex molecules (e.g., sugars, starches) into simpler compounds that can be absorbed by the body.\n10. **Gasification**: Heating materials (e.g., biomass, coal) in the presence of oxygen to produce a mixture of gases (e.g., hydrogen, carbon monoxide) that can be converted into fuels, chemicals, or other products.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': "Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Converting the given substances into absorbable forms:\n\n1. Plastic beach trash (e.g., plastic bags, bottles, microbeads) \n- Heat process: Pyrolysis (break down into oil, gas, and carbon) or Thermal decomposition (break down into smaller molecules)\n- Chemical process: Chemical depolymerization (break down into monomers)\n\n2. Dead or unconscious animals (e.g., fish, birds, mammals)\n- Heat process: Incineration (break down into ash, gas, and water vapor)\n- Chemical process: Autoclaving (high-temperature steam to break down proteins and fats)\n\n3. Dark coat and hat (made of synthetic materials)\n- Heat process: Pyrolysis (break down into oil, gas, and carbon)\n- Chemical process: Chemical depolymerization (break down into monomers)\n\n4. Green object (e.g., seaweed, grass)\n- Heat process: Drying (remove moisture, preserve nutrients)\n- Chemical process: Enzymatic hydrolysis (break down into simpler compounds)\n\n5. Sushi (made of fish, rice, and seaweed)\n- Heat process: Cooking (heat denatures proteins, gelatinizes starches)\n- Chemical process: Enzymatic hydrolysis (break down into simpler compounds)\n\n6. Dog's waste (e.g., feces, urine)\n- Heat process: Incineration (break down into ash, gas, and water vapor)\n- Chemical process: Chemical treatment (e.g., using bleach or other disinfectants to break down pathogens)"}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Convert into bioavailable nutrients through thermal decomposition or enzymatic hydrolysis.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Break down into digestible nutrients, such as through thermal or enzymatic digestion.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: To convert various substances into absorbable forms, the following processes can be considered:\n\n1. Starch (complex carbohydrate) - Converted into Maltodextrin (a simple carbohydrate) through a heat process involving enzymes and acid hydrolysis.\n2. Fiber (complex polysaccharide) - Converted into Pectin (a soluble fiber) through a heat process involving enzymes and acid hydrolysis.\n3. Protein (complex protein) - Converted into Peptides (short chains of amino acids) through a chemical process involving enzymes and acid hydrolysis.\n4. Fats (triglycerides) - Converted into Glycerol (a simple sugar) through a heat process involving enzymes and acid hydrolysis.\n5. Cellulose (complex polysaccharide) - Converted into Glucose (a simple sugar) through a chemical process involving enzymes and acid hydrolysis.\n\nNote: The exact process and conditions may vary depending on the specific substance and the desired product.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Converting various substances into absorbable forms often involves breaking down complex molecules into simpler ones that can be easily digested by the body. Here are some examples:\n\n1. **Cellulose (plant cell walls) to glucose**: Heat, enzymes, or chemical processes can break down cellulose into glucose, a simple sugar that can be absorbed by the body.\n\n2. **Lignin (plant lignin) to water and carbon dioxide**: Heat, enzymes, or chemical processes can break down lignin into water and carbon dioxide, making it easier to absorb.\n\n3. **Silica (sand) to silicic acid**: Chemical processes, such as acid hydrolysis, can convert silica into silicic acid, which can be absorbed by the body.\n\n4. **Calcium carbonate (limestone) to calcium ions**: Heat, acids, or chemical processes can break down calcium carbonate into calcium ions, which can be absorbed by the body.\n\n5. **Protein (animal or plant-based) to amino acids**: Enzymes or chemical processes can break down proteins into individual amino acids, which can be absorbed by the body.\n\n6. **Fat (triglycerides) to fatty acids and glycerol**: Enzymes or chemical processes can break down triglycerides into fatty acids and glycerol, which can be absorbed by the body.\n\n7. **Starch (carbohydrates) to maltose and glucose**: Enzymes, such as amylase, can break down starch into maltose and glucose, which can be absorbed by the body.\n\nThese are just a few examples of how various substances can be converted into absorbable forms using heat, enzymes, or chemical processes.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Convert them into absorbable substances using heat or a chemical process.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Convert them into absorbable substances through heat or chemical treatment.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: become completely focused on a partic